<p>Depending on the printer you are using, the available items may vary.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: Leave Blank</span></p>
<p>Inserts a blank sheet as a separator from a different tray selected 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> before the page specified 
 in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span>.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: One Side</span></p>
<p>Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span> 
 on a chapter cover from the tray selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Input 
 Tray:</span>. If you enable this setting, sheets will be printed on the 
 front side only, even if you have specified 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Designate: Both Sides</span></p>
<p>Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span> 
 on the front side of a chapter cover from a different tray selected in 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Input Tray:</span> and the next page on the back 
 side. This option is for 2 sided printing.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Chapter</span></p>
<p>Prints the page specified in <span class="Term-Soft">Page Number:</span> 
 on the front side of the sheet at all times while in 2 sided print mode. 
 With this selection, you will be unable to use a different input tray 
 setting than the other pages.</p>
